    "text": "The program below is a greedy heuristic, not a proven optimum. It repeatedly places the router with the best ratio of newly covered targets to connection-plus-router cost, and it respects the budget and every validity rule. I have not compiled or run it, and I did not benchmark it against the 10-second limit.\n\n**How it works**\n\n- **Coverage:** 2D prefix sums of wall cells give an O(1) check for whether a router's line of sight to a target is blocked.\n- **Gains:** each candidate cell's gain (uncovered targets it would cover) is computed once and decremented incrementally as targets get covered.\n- **Connection cost:** a 0-1 BFS from the connected set gives each cell the number of new cells needed to reach it. The BFS parent chain is a valid path, so connecting a router means adding that chain outward from the backbone.\n- **Selection:** a max-heap keyed by gain/cost is popped lazily. Keys are re-checked with exact costs before accepting, and the BFS is rebuilt every 64 placements or when the heap empties.\n- **Output order:** each connected chain is emitted from the backbone outward, so every listed cell neighbours an earlier one.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint H, W, R;\nlong long Pb, Pr, B;\nvector<char> g;\nvector<int> P;\nint WP;\nvector<int> gain;\nvector<char> covered, inS, used;\nvector<int> dist_, par_;\nconst int INF = 1000000000;\n\ninline bool covers(int a, int b, int x, int y) {\n    int r1 = min(a, x), r2 = max(a, x), c1 = min(b, y), c2 = max(b, y);\n    int s = P[(r2 + 1) * WP + (c2 + 1)] - P[r1 * WP + (c2 + 1)]\n          - P[(r2 + 1) * WP + c1] + P[r1 * WP + c1];\n    return s == 0;\n}\n\nvoid markTarget(int t) {\n    covered[t] = 1;\n    int x = t / W, y = t % W;\n    for (int a = max(0, x - R); a <= min(H - 1, x + R); a++)\n        for (int b = max(0, y - R); b <= min(W - 1, y + R); b++) {\n            int c = a * W + b;\n            if (g[c] == '#') continue;\n            if (covers(a, b, x, y)) gain[c]--;\n        }\n}\n\nvoid bfs(const vector<int>& dummy) {\n    (void)dummy;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    cin >> H >> W >> R;\n    cin >> Pb >> Pr >> B;\n    int br, bc;\n    cin >> br >> bc;\n    g.assign((size_t)H * W, '-');\n    for (int r = 0; r < H; r++) {\n        string s;\n        cin >> s;\n        for (int c = 0; c < W; c++) g[r * W + c] = s[c];\n    }\n\n    WP = W + 1;\n    P.assign((size_t)(H + 1) * WP, 0);\n    for (int r = 0; r < H; r++)\n        for (int c = 0; c < W; c++) {\n            int w = (g[r * W + c] == '#') ? 1 : 0;\n            P[(r + 1) * WP + (c + 1)] = P[r * WP + (c + 1)] + P[(r + 1) * WP + c] - P[r * WP + c] + w;\n        }\n\n    int NN = H * W;\n    gain.assign(NN, 0);\n    covered.assign(NN, 0);\n    inS.assign(NN, 0);\n    used.assign(NN, 0);\n    dist_.assign(NN, INF);\n    par_.assign(NN, -1);\n\n    for (int a = 0; a < H; a++)\n        for (int b = 0; b < W; b++) {\n            int c = a * W + b;\n            if (g[c] == '#') continue;\n            int cnt = 0;\n            for (int x = max(0, a - R); x <= min(H - 1, a + R); x++)\n                for (int y = max(0, b - R); y <= min(W - 1, b + R); y++) {\n                    if (g[x * W + y] == '.' && covers(a, b, x, y)) cnt++;\n                }\n            gain[c] = cnt;\n        }\n\n    int init = br * W + bc;\n    inS[init] = 1;\n\n    vector<int> order;\n    vector<int> routers;\n    long long spent = 0;\n\n    auto bfsRun = [&]() {\n        fill(dist_.begin(), dist_.end(), INF);\n        deque<int> dq;\n        for (int i = 0; i < NN; i++)\n            if (inS[i]) { dist_[i] = 0; dq.push_back(i); }\n        while (!dq.empty()) {\n            int u = dq.front(); dq.pop_front();\n            int ua = u / W, ub = u % W;\n            for (int da = -1; da <= 1; da++)\n                for (int db = -1; db <= 1; db++) {\n                    if (da == 0 && db == 0) continue;\n                    int va = ua + da, vb = ub + db;\n                    if (va < 0 || va >= H || vb < 0 || vb >= W) continue;\n                    int v = va * W + vb;\n                    int w = inS[v] ? 0 : 1;\n                    int nd = dist_[u] + w;\n                    if (nd < dist_[v]) {\n                        dist_[v] = nd;\n                        par_[v] = u;\n                        if (w == 0) dq.push_front(v); else dq.push_back(v);\n                    }\n                }\n        }\n    };\n\n    vector<pair<double, int>> heap;\n    auto rebuild = [&]() {\n        bfsRun();\n        heap.clear();\n        for (int id = 0; id < NN; id++) {\n            if (g[id] == '#' || used[id] || dist_[id] >= INF || gain[id] <= 0) continue;\n            long long cost = (long long)dist_[id] * Pb + Pr;\n            if (spent + cost > B) continue;\n            heap.push_back({(double)gain[id] / (double)cost, id});\n        }\n        make_heap(heap.begin(), heap.end());\n    };\n\n    rebuild();\n    int since = 0;\n    vector<int> chain;\n    while (true) {\n        if (since >= 64 || heap.empty()) {\n            if (heap.empty() && since == 0) break;\n            rebuild();\n            since = 0;\n            if (heap.empty()) break;\n        }\n        pop_heap(heap.begin(), heap.end());\n        int c = heap.back().second;\n        heap.pop_back();\n        if (used[c] || gain[c] <= 0) continue;\n        if (dist_[c] >= INF) continue;\n\n        chain.clear();\n        int cur = c;\n        while (!inS[cur]) {\n            chain.push_back(cur);\n            cur = par_[cur];\n        }\n        int k = (int)chain.size();\n        long long cost = (long long)k * Pb + Pr;\n        if (spent + cost > B) continue;\n        double r = (double)gain[c] / (double)cost;\n        if (!heap.empty() && r < heap.front().first) {\n            heap.push_back({r, c});\n            push_heap(heap.begin(), heap.end());\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = k - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n            inS[chain